  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to establishing\ndistinctive \"Alzheimer's Awareness\" license plates; and to amend the state\nfinance law, in relation to providing for further funding for the \"Alzheimer's\ndisease assistance fund\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S6400",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6400-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 42,
       "fullName": "Jen Metzger",
       "imgName": "1054_Jen_Metzger.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1234,
       "sessionMemberId": 1232,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "METZGER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-ff, V & T L; amd §89-e, St Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6400\n\nSPONSOR: LANZA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to establishing distinctive \"Alzheimer's Awareness\" license\nplates; and to amend the state finance law, in relation to providing for\nfurther funding for the \"Alzheimer's disease assistance fund\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo establish a distinctive Alzheimer's Awareness license plates and\nproviding that the funding for such be deposited in the Alzheimer's\ndisease assistance fund.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the vehicle and traffic law by adding a new section\n404-ff.\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision 2 of section 89-e of the state finance law,\nas amended by chapter 359 of the laws of 2002.\n\nSection 3 states that such distinctive plate established pursuant to\nsection 404-ff be designed, produced and issued by the New York State\nDepartment of Motor Vehicles.\n\nSection 4 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFor many people on the Alzheimer's journey most of the time it feels\nlike a roller coaster of ups and downs. Alzheimer's not only has a trau-\nmatic effect on the person diagnosed with this disease but it takes its\ntoll on family members who have to care for their loved one.  As New\nYorkers, we need to stick together and fight this dreadful disease and\nfind a cure. Until this day comes, we must educate the public through\ncommunity outreach and awareness. This bill would establish a distinc-\ntive Alzheimer's Awareness license plate and provide a funding stream\nfor the State's Alzheimer's Disease Assistance Fund. This fund promotes\npublic awareness and education about Alzheimer's. While many families\nhave lost a love one or know someone with Alzheimer's, the family of the\nlate Joe Savino from Staten Island who lost his life to Alzheimer's\nbelieve awareness, education and research is the key in combating this\ndisease. To accomplish this goal, creating a New York State distinctive\nAlzheimer's Awareness license plate is a positive step toward raising\nfunds and public awareness of this terrible disease.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
